    "Month 1: Oil production kicks in quickly — skin may feel greasier within weeks. Acne often follows.\n\nMonths 3–5: Body hair begins appearing in a predictable pattern: lower legs → thighs → abdomen." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Month 1: Oil production kicks in quickly — skin may feel greasier within weeks. Acne often follows.\n\nMonths 3–5: Body hair begins appearing in a predictable pattern: lower legs → thighs → abdomen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Month 1: Reduced oiliness is often the very first change — noticeable within weeks." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Month 1: Reduced oiliness is often the very first change — noticeable within weeks."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 1–3: Early strength gains — you may notice exercises feeling easier. Some water retention can give a 'fuller' look.\n\nMonths 3–5: Noticeable muscle growth, especially upper body. Recovery between workouts improves significantly." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 1–3: Early strength gains — you may notice exercises feeling easier. Some water retention can give a 'fuller' look.\n\nMonths 3–5: Noticeable muscle growth, especially upper body. Recovery between workouts improves significantly."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 1–3: Emotional sensitivity often increases first. You may feel more tearful, reactive, or emotionally open. This is neurochemical recalibration.\n\nMonths 3–6: Emotional range broadens. Many describe feeling 'more themselves' — a sense of emotional alignment that was missing before." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 1–3: Emotional sensitivity often increases first. You may feel more tearful, reactive, or emotionally open. This is neurochemical recalibration.\n\nMonths 3–6: Emotional range broadens. Many describe feeling 'more themselves' — a sense of emotional alignment that was missing before."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 1–3: Subtle — you may notice slight softening around the hips or face.\n\nMonths 3–5: Fat redistribution becomes visible. Pants may fit differently as hip and thigh circumference increases." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 1–3: Subtle — you may notice slight softening around the hips or face.\n\nMonths 3–5: Fat redistribution becomes visible. Pants may fit differently as hip and thigh circumference increases."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 1–3: You may feel a scratchy throat or notice slight hoarseness — the first signs of vocal fold thickening.\n\nMonths 3–5: The first noticeable pitch drop typically happens here. Voice may crack or feel unstable." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 1–3: You may feel a scratchy throat or notice slight hoarseness — the first signs of vocal fold thickening.\n\nMonths 3–5: The first noticeable pitch drop typically happens here. Voice may crack or feel unstable."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 2–5: Skin texture begins softening. Pores appear smaller, hydration improves." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 2–5: Skin texture begins softening. Pores appear smaller, hydration improves."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 6–12: Body hair continues filling in (chest, back, face). Acne may peak during this period." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 6–12: Body hair continues filling in (chest, back, face). Acne may peak during this period."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 6–12: Continuing gradual drop. Your voice is settling into its new range." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 6–12: Continuing gradual drop. Your voice is settling into its new range."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 6–12: Mood patterns stabilise as your brain adapts to the new hormonal environment. Cyclical trough effects may become noticeable." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 6–12: Mood patterns stabilise as your brain adapts to the new hormonal environment. Cyclical trough effects may become noticeable."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 6–12: Strength continues increasing. Body composition is visibly shifting toward more lean mass." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 6–12: Strength continues increasing. Body composition is visibly shifting toward more lean mass."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 6–12: The 'glow' becomes apparent. Skin is noticeably softer and more radiant than pre-HRT." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 6–12: The 'glow' becomes apparent. Skin is noticeably softer and more radiant than pre-HRT."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 6–12: Waist-to-hip ratio begins shifting noticeably. Upper body muscle loss contributes to a narrower shoulder appearance." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 6–12: Waist-to-hip ratio begins shifting noticeably. Upper body muscle loss contributes to a narrower shoulder appearance."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 12–24: Body and facial hair continue filling in. Acne typically begins to mellow. Scalp hairline may stabilise or continue receding depending on genetics." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 12–24: Body and facial hair continue filling in. Acne typically begins to mellow. Scalp hairline may stabilise or continue receding depending on genetics."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 12–24: Most of the deepening is done. Any remaining changes are very subtle. Your speaking voice has found its natural pitch." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 12–24: Most of the deepening is done. Any remaining changes are very subtle. Your speaking voice has found its natural pitch."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 12–24: Muscle growth velocity peaks. Without training, you'll maintain above-baseline lean mass. With training, this is peak gain season." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 12–24: Muscle growth velocity peaks. Without training, you'll maintain above-baseline lean mass. With training, this is peak gain season."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 12–24: The bulk of your fat redistribution is complete. Your silhouette has changed meaningfully. Any remaining shifts are slow and subtle — fat cells turn over on a ~2–3 year cycle." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 12–24: The bulk of your fat redistribution is complete. Your silhouette has changed meaningfully. Any remaining shifts are slow and subtle — fat cells turn over on a ~2–3 year cycle."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 12–24: The emotional baseline typically settles and holds. Patterns across a dose cycle are usually recognisable by this point." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 12–24: The emotional baseline typically settles and holds. Patterns across a dose cycle are usually recognisable by this point."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Months 12–24: Your skin has fully transitioned. Collagen density is up, sebum is down, and the texture difference from pre-HRT is complete." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Months 12–24: Your skin has fully transitioned. Collagen density is up, sebum is down, and the texture difference from pre-HRT is complete."
          }
        }
      }
    },
