    "Skin aging continues on its normal course. Skin remains softer than it would be without estrogen, but photoaging and age-related collagen loss are universal. Retinoids, vitamin C and sun protection are the interventions with evidence behind them." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Skin aging continues on its normal course. Skin remains softer than it would be without estrogen, but photoaging and age-related collagen loss are universal. Retinoids, vitamin C and sun protection are the interventions with evidence behind them."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Skin changes are largely complete by this stage. No hormone-specific intervention is indicated." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Skin changes are largely complete by this stage. No hormone-specific intervention is indicated."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Skin typically continues softening over the next several months, and acne typically continues decreasing. Estrogen-thinned skin is more UV-sensitive than it was before therapy." : {
      "localizations" : {
